601	    // wrapped allocator. The concrete type of this object depends on
602	    // the type of this->device, so eigen_gpu_device can't be an
603	    // inline member and must be heap allocated. However, we don't
604	    // want to allocate a new eigen_gpu_device for every Op that is
605	    // executed. Instead this member is allocated on first use using
606	    // ensure_eigen_gpu_device, and then if the Params structure is
607	    // re-used for subsequent Ops, the eigen_gpu_device is
608	    // ReInitialized in the OpKernelContext constructor. Unlike the
609	    // other pointers in Params, this one is owned by Params.
